claim.claim-text:
delivering, by a drive circuit, an energy signal to a surgical instrument;
measuring tissue impedance of tissue engaged with the surgical instrument;
ceasing delivery of the energy signal upon the tissue impedance matching a threshold impedance value;
estimating at least one tissue parameter based at least partially on the measured tissue impedance of the tissue;
generating a parameterized tissue model based on the at least one estimated tissue parameter; and
generating a control technique for delivery of the energy signal based on the parameterized tissue model.

a processor;
an end effector at a distal end of the surgical instrument, the end effector configured to interact with tissue, the end effector comprising:
a clamp arm comprising an electrode;
an ultrasonic blade;

control delivery of RF energy to the electrode or ultrasonic energy to the ultrasonic blade;
measure tissue impedance of tissue engaged with the end effector;
cease delivery of RF energy to the electrode or ultrasonic energy to the ultrasonic blade upon the tissue impedance matching a threshold impedance value;
estimate at least one tissue parameter based at least partially on the measured tissue impedance of the tissue;
generate a parameterized tissue model based on the at least one estimated tissue parameter; and
generate a control technique for delivery of RF energy to the electrode or ultrasonic energy to the ultrasonic blade based on the parameterized tissue model.

a first drive circuit configured to deliver a drive signal to an ultrasonic transducer;
a second drive circuit configured to deliver radio frequency (RF) energy to the electrode; and
a processor configured to control the first drive circuit and the second drive circuit, and wherein the processor is configured to:

control the second drive circuit to deliver RF energy to the electrode or the first drive circuit to deliver ultrasonic energy to the ultrasonic blade;
measure tissue impedance of tissue engaged with the end effector;
cease delivery of RF energy to the electrode or ultrasonic energy to the ultrasonic blade upon the tissue impedance matching a threshold impedance value;
estimate at least one tissue parameter based at least partially on the measured tissue impedance of the tissue;
generate a parameterized tissue model based on the at least one estimated tissue parameter; and
generate a control technique for delivery of RF energy to the electrode or ultrasonic energy to the ultrasonic blade based on the parameterized tissue model.
